    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d595">

                <pb facs="0613" n="607" sameAs="frus:frus1894app1/pg607"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Gresham to Sir
                            Julian Pauncefote.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1893-10-27"><hi rendition="#italic">October 27,
                        1893</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge with
                    thanks the receipt of your note of the 24th instant, transmitting a copy of a
                    dispatch, together with its accompaniments, which the Earl of Rosebery has
                    addressed to Her Majesty’s chargé d’affaires at Berlin respecting the
                    deportation of Mataafa and other chiefs from Samoa.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">W. Q. Gresham.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
